 "notes": "95% CL 'M87 (95% c.l.)' contour of Figure 6 (file Bayesian.pdf in the e-print), the paper's stated main result, for the benchmark Virgo magnetic-field model (B0=31.5 muG); flat level 1.49e-12 GeV^-1 for ma<~1e-13 eV matches Eq. (5.3). Curve extracted from vector paths; axes calibrated with decade tick marks and cross-checked against the SN1987A line, which lands at 5.3e-12 GeV^-1 as quoted. Curve spans the plotted range 1e-14 to 1.2e-11 eV; the flat low-mass bound extends below 1e-14 eV. The abstract also quotes a weaker, more conservative bound of 2.6e-12 GeV^-1 from alternative B-field model 2 (B0=35 muG, alpha=0.67, Fig. 10 right); the benchmark Fig. 6 curve is reported here as the headline. Not a dark-matter search, so no rho_DM rescaling.",
